IntentExecutionPolicy::checkAction
├── given target is whitelisted
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS (regardless of selector/spender)
├── given target is not whitelisted
│   ├── given selector is approve(address,uint256)
│   │   ├── given spender is paymaster
│   │   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
│   │   ├── given spender is a whitelisted address
│   │   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
│   │   ├── given spender is not paymaster or whitelisted
│   │   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
│   │   └── given calldata is too short (no spender argument)
│   │       └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
│   └── given selector is not approve
│       └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
└── given calldata is empty or less than 4 bytes
    └── it should fall through to VALIDATION_FAILED for non-whitelisted target
